Chapter: ReservoirUniformTest
  cites AI chapter Reservoir

 Reservoir sampling promises one thing: after streaming n items through a
 reservoir of capacity k, every item that went past has the same probability
 of being in the sample. Not a similar probability. The same one. That is the
 whole reason to use Algorithm R rather than keeping the first k.

 `reservoir-rand` was `bit-xor (seed * 2654435761) (n * 40503)` and then a
 remainder by n, with no downward fold. Multiplication carries entropy upward
 only, so the keep-or-drop decision at position n was a function of the low
 bits of the seed and of n. A sampler whose acceptance is a parity stripe is
 not sampling; it is applying a fixed rule and calling the result random.

 The measurement is the promise. Stream the same twenty items through a
 five-slot reservoir under many different seeds and count how often each item
 survives. Uniform sampling puts every item in the sample about a quarter of
 the time. A structured one favours some positions and starves others, and
 the spread between the luckiest and the unluckiest item is what shows it.

Section: Fixtures

  rut-items : Integer
  rut-items = 20

  rut-cap : Integer
  rut-cap = 5

  rut-trials : Integer
  rut-trials = 200

  rut-stream : Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  rut-stream (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else rut-stream (i + 1) n (list-push acc i)

  rut-zeros : Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  rut-zeros (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else rut-zeros (i + 1) n (list-push acc 0)

Section: Trials

 Each trial builds a fresh reservoir: reservoir-add writes surviving slots
 with list-set-at, which mutates in place, so a reused one would carry the
 previous trial's contents.

  rut-tally-one : List Integer, List Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  rut-tally-one (counts) (sample) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then counts
    else let v = list-at sample i
    in rut-tally-one (list-set-at counts v (list-at counts v + 1)) sample (i + 1) n

  rut-run : List Integer, List Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  rut-run (counts) (stream) (t) (n) =
    if t >= n then counts
    else let rs = reservoir-add-all (reservoir-new rut-cap) stream (t * 7919 + 13) 0 rut-items
    in let s = reservoir-items rs
    in rut-run (rut-tally-one counts s 0 (list-length s)) stream (t + 1) n

Section: Checks

  rut-min : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rut-min (xs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else let v = list-at xs i
    in rut-min xs (i + 1) n (if v < acc then v else acc)

  rut-max : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rut-max (xs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else let v = list-at xs i
    in rut-max xs (i + 1) n (if v > acc then v else acc)

  rut-sum : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rut-sum (xs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else rut-sum xs (i + 1) n (acc + list-at xs i)

  rut-fmt : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  rut-fmt (xs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else let sep = if i == 0 then "" else " "
    in rut-fmt xs (i + 1) n (acc & sep & show (list-at xs i))

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing =
    let stream = rut-stream 0 rut-items []
    in let counts = rut-run (rut-zeros 0 rut-items []) stream 0 rut-trials
    in let lo = rut-min counts 0 rut-items 999999
    in let hi = rut-max counts 0 rut-items 0
    in let tot = rut-sum counts 0 rut-items 0
    in act
      print-line-uni ("counts:      " & rut-fmt counts 0 rut-items "")
      print-line-uni ("expected ea: " & show (rut-trials * rut-cap / rut-items))
      print-line-uni ("min:         " & show lo)
      print-line-uni ("max:         " & show hi)
      print-line-uni ("total:       " & show tot)
      print-line-uni ("all sampled: " & show (lo > 0))
      print-line-uni ("within 2x:   " & show (hi <= lo * 2))
    end
